👉 Notice karo:
Static block sirf ek baar chala (class load hone par).
Har object ke liye pehle instance initializer block chala, phir constructor.
------------------------------------------------------------------------
As we know that whether it is static final variable;(static variables -They are always available at the class load time only).
Or final variable; (non static variable will be available at the time of the object creation not at the static time or class load time).
So these both static and non-static have different checkpoints to initialize them.

Static final → initialize kar sakte ho:
a. declaration ke time
b. static initializer block

Instance final (non‑static) → initialize kar sakte ho:
a. declaration ke time
b. instance initializer block
c. constructor


Accha suno inhe JVM initialize nahi karta default values se, final keyword walo ko JVM touch nahi karta default values dene ke liye,
becuase agar de diya toh firr wo default ka hi hoke reh jayega, kyuki wo final h, so jo pehle de diya wahi
